// ============================================================================
// Hunt: Warlock ransomware TTPs — BYOVD K7RKScan driver, VS Code tunnel C2,
//       ransomware staged in SYSVOL
// Context: Per Symantec reporting in the October 12, 2026 brief, the
//   China-linked Warlock operation (aka Longlegs / Storm-2603) breached at
//   least four organizations (water utility, telecom, regional government,
//   university) over two months ending Oct 1, 2026, reusing the on-premises
//   SharePoint ToolShell chain (CVE-2025-49704, CVE-2025-49706,
//   CVE-2025-53770, CVE-2025-53771 — 15 months patchable) alongside newer
//   CVE-2026-45659 (now in CISA KEV). In one intrusion (Jul 22-31), a
//   vulnerable K7RKScan driver (BYOVD) was used to kill endpoint protection
//   on at least 40 hosts within about two hours; Warlock ransomware was
//   then staged in the domain SYSVOL share and deployed to 33 hosts. The
//   group also uses Visual Studio Code tunnels for command and control.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1190 (Exploit Public-Facing Application),
//               T1562.001 (Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools),
//               T1572 (Protocol Tunneling),
//               T1486 (Data Encrypted for Impact)
// Data: Microsoft Defender - DeviceImageLoadEvents, DeviceProcessEvents,
//       DeviceFileEvents
// Write-up: https://amitvijayan.com/journal/articles/daily-cyber-threat-brief-october-12-2026.html
// Logic: a driver named K7RKScan.sys should never load; 'code tunnel'
//   command lines on hosts that should not run VS Code are the C2 staging
//   Warlock used; executables landing in SYSVOL written by non-replication
//   processes are the deployment vector.
// ============================================================================

// -- Variant 1: BYOVD — vulnerable K7RKScan driver loaded (EDR killer)
DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where FileName endswith "K7RKScan.sys"
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, FileName, SHA256,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessCommandLine
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// -- Variant 2: VS Code tunnel used as C2 channel
DeviceProcessEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where ProcessCommandLine has "code tunnel"
   or ProcessCommandLine has "code-tunnel"
   or FileName =~ "code-tunnel.exe"
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, AccountName, InitiatingProcessAccountName,
          FileName, ProcessCommandLine
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// -- Variant 3: ransomware staged in the domain SYSVOL share
DeviceFileEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where FolderPath has "SYSVOL"
| where ActionType in ("FileCreated", "FileModified")
| where FileName endswith ".exe" or FileName endswith ".ps1"
   or FileName endswith ".bat" or FileName endswith ".msi"
| summarize Writers = make_set(InitiatingProcessFileName, 10),
            FileCount = count(),
            Files = make_set(FileName, 20),
            FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated),
            LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated)
    by DeviceName, FolderPath
| where Writers !has "dfsr.exe"      // exclude legitimate DFS replication
| order by LastSeen desc
